  :adr/language-extension-implementation-2026-07-14
  {:summary "Implemented the :add-verdict items from :adr/triage in
             kotoba-lang/compiler's frontend.clj: and/or/when (ported from
             kotoba-lang/kotoba's proven desugar-and/desugar-or) + keyword
             literals + map literals + get/assoc. Destructuring/vectors/
             multi-arity/loop-recur (also :add in the triage) NOT
             implemented this pass -- scoped to the highest-value subset
             plus the trivial and/or/when port."
   :decisive-design-discovery
   "backend/wasm.clj's `emit` already imports pair/pair-first/pair-second
    as HOST FUNCTIONS (kotoba:heap.pair/pair-first/pair-second) -- they are
    NOT guest-managed WASM linear memory. This means map/keyword required
    ZERO backend/codegen changes: purely frontend desugaring to the
    existing primitives, automatically working across all 3 target
    backends (wasm32/x86_64/aarch64) since each already implements the
    same pair-family host-injection mechanism on its own side."
   :implementation
   {:and-or-when "ported verbatim in spirit from kotoba-lang/kotoba's
                   runtime.clj desugar-and/desugar-or (live-verified
                   correct there earlier this session); when has no `do`
                   in this profile (compiler/ never had one) -- test +
                   exactly one result expression only"
    :keyword "deterministic 64-bit FNV-1a hash of the keyword's string
              form, interned as an i64 constant -- NOT clojure.core/hash
              (unspecified long-term stability), chosen to match this
              compiler's byte-for-byte reproducible-build gates"
    :map "{:k1 v1 :k2 v2} desugars to (pair (pair k1' v1') (pair (pair k2'
          v2') 0)) reusing the existing pair/list primitives entirely;
          entries sorted by (pr-str k) for deterministic codegen
          regardless of Clojure's own unordered map-literal iteration"
    :get "compiler-synthesized recursive helper __kotoba_map_get, injected
          into a module's function set ONLY when actually used (post-
          desugar AST scan) -- linear-scans the pair-list; each recursive
          step costs 1 unit of the EXISTING fixed 256-call fuel budget
          (unmodified) -- map-walk depth is now bounded by that same
          pre-existing mechanism, not a new limit"
    :assoc "pure O(1) desugar: prepend (pair k' v') in front of the map
            value; variadic k/v pairs supported; shadows (not removes) an
            existing key -- get returns the newest via first-match, older
            entries are dead weight, not corrected, documented tradeoff"}
   :verification
   {:oracle-interpreter "ir.clj's execute via compile-source's :oracle-value
                          -- and/or/when, map+get (hit/miss/explicit-
                          default), assoc+get, assoc-shadow all correct"
    :real-chicory-execution
    "scratch verification (not committed, matches compiler/'s own
     convention of not depending on Chicory in its test suite): compiled
     the SAME source strings to actual WASM bytes, built a real Chicory
     Instance with genuine host-side HostFunction implementations of
     kotoba:heap.pair/pair-first/pair-second, called the main export
     directly. Results matched the oracle exactly for every scenario --
     confirms the emitted binary is correct, not just the compiler's own
     internal reference interpreter"
    :test-suite "clojure -M:test: 96 tests / 2725 assertions (80
                 pre-existing + 16 new in frontend_extensions_test.clj),
                 0 failures. Existing fuzz/property test suites
                 (frontend-fuzz-test/security-fuzz-test/property-test)
                 unaffected -- grammar expansion did not break generative
                 testing against the wider admission surface"}
   :honest-limitations
   ["assoc never removes shadowed entries -- monotonic growth under
     repeated re-assoc of the same key, documented not fixed"
    "map literal entry count reuses the existing max-list-items (128)
     bound -- combined with get's 1-fuel-per-step cost this means a
     LITERAL map's full miss-walk (128+1=129) never actually reaches the
     256-fuel ceiling; fuel exhaustion via map operations is only
     reachable through dynamic growth via repeated assoc in a recursive
     helper, which the test suite demonstrates directly rather than via a
     giant map literal (which the entry-count bound would reject first)"
    "compiler/README.md's stale 'no when/do/and/or sugar' line corrected in
     the same commit -- do remains unsupported, and/or/when now are"
    "kotoba-lang/kotoba (wasm_exec.clj) was NOT given the same map/keyword
     treatment in this pass -- unlike compiler/, it has no pair/heap
     primitive at all yet (confirmed by this session's earlier grammar
     survey), so adding map/keyword there is a larger prerequisite task,
     explicitly deferred"]
