  :adr/kotoba-lang-kotoba-implementation-2026-07-14
  {:summary "Owner decided (after being told kotoba-lang/kotoba has no safety
             gate) to implement map/keyword there too, for kotoba/'s own
             expressiveness independent of the safety motivation. Implemented
             pair/pair-first/pair-second + keyword/map literals + get/assoc
             in kotoba.runtime/compile-wasm-expr."
   :architectural-difference-from-compiler
   "compiler/'s pair is a host-imported capability (established in the
    language-extension-implementation addendum above). kotoba/ already
    exposes raw linear memory to guest code directly (alloc/i32-store!/
    mem-i32-at pre-exist) -- so pair needed ZERO new opcodes or host
    imports, just a desugar to let+alloc+existing store/load ops. 8 bytes
    per pair: left i32 @ offset 0, right i32 @ offset 4."
   :get-implementation-difference-from-compiler
   "compiler/'s get is a synthesized recursive helper injected once per
    module. kotoba/'s function-defs is consumed from 4 separate call
    sites with no single injection point analogous to compiler/'s
    analyze -- so get here is a BOUNDED UNROLL (fixed depth 32, m/k/
    default each let-bound once so the unrolled body only re-references
    cheap locals) instead. A miss past that depth returns the default
    silently rather than trapping (compiler/'s fuel-bounded recursive
    version traps instead) -- a real, documented difference in failure
    mode, not a bug."
   :keyword-hash "32-bit FNV-1a (kotoba/'s default numeric domain is i32,
                  vs compiler/'s i64) -- same deterministic-hash rationale
                  as compiler/'s version"
   :verification
   {:method "kotoba.runtime/wasm-binary + kotoba.wasm-exec/run-main -- the
             SAME real compile -> emit -> Chicory-execute path
             wasm-and-or-when-test/wasm-exec-test already use, not a
             separate scratch script"
