  :adr/compiler-destructuring-vector-loop-implementation-2026-07-14
  {:summary "Implemented the remaining :add-verdict items in kotoba-lang/
             compiler's frontend.clj: destructuring (let + defn params,
             one level only), vector-as-data (reuses desugar-list's
             pair-chain encoding), and loop/recur (synthesized recursive
             helper + purely-syntactic free-variable capture). Multi-arity
             defn -- also :add in the triage -- explicitly deferred: unlike
             every other item here it is NOT frontend-only (would require
             changing signatures' shape, validate-expr's call-arity
             resolution, AND all 3 backends' WASM export-naming, since WASM
             has no function-name overloading)."
   :bugs-found-and-fixed
   [{:bug "let's generic default desugar case called desugar-expr on the
           WHOLE bindings vector as one opaque arg -- vectors aren't seq?,
           so it passed through unchanged, silently skipping map/keyword/
           vector desugaring of binding VALUES"
     :symptom "(let [m {:a 1}] (get m :a)) failed: \"value type is outside
               the safe profile\" -- live-confirmed before the fix"
     :fix "added a dedicated `let` case to desugar-expr's dispatch:
           destructure-binding expands each pattern, each binding VALUE is
           explicitly desugar-expr'd"}
    {:bug "loop-helper's synthesized function name used gensym (a JVM-
           process-global monotonic counter) -- safe for let-local temp
           names (erased to WASM local indices, as and/or's gensym'd temps
           already proved) but NOT for this exported top-level function
           name, baked literally into the WASM export section"
     :symptom "compiling the same loop-using source twice in one process
               produced DIFFERENT bytes (oracle value correct and IDENTICAL
               both times -- only the byte-level export name differed),
               violating this compiler's byte-for-byte reproducible-build
               gate. Live-confirmed before the fix."
     :fix "replaced gensym with a deterministic *loop-counter* (a volatile!
           dynamic var), bound ONCE per top-level analyze call, incremented
           sequentially -- deterministic because the same source is always
           desugared in the same left-to-right order"}
    {:bug "surfaced while fixing the above: let's body used a bare (map
           desugar-expr body), a lazy seq, passed as list*'s FINAL argument
           -- list* never forces its tail. This deferred the actual
           desugar-expr calls (and therefore the (vswap! *loop-counter*
           inc) inside any nested loop) past the end of *loop-counter*'s
           `binding` scope, to whenever something later happened to force
           that lazy seq (e.g. uses-map-get?'s post-analyze tree walk)"
     :symptom "NullPointerException: Cannot invoke Volatile.deref() because
               the return value of Var.get() is null -- *loop-counter* back
               at its nil default by the time the lazy seq was finally
               forced. Live-confirmed before the fix, only reproducible
               with a `loop` nested inside a `let` body."
     :fix "replaced (map desugar-expr body) with (mapv desugar-expr body)
           -- eager, forces immediately within the correct dynamic scope.
           Manually audited every other map/mapcat/concat/cons combination
           in frontend.clj for the same lazy-tail-into-list*/cons pattern;
           found no other instance (desugar-list/desugar-map/the generic
           default case's `apply list` all force eagerly already)"}]
   :honest-limitations
   ["destructuring's gensym'd let-local temp names (destr-map__NNN etc) are
     a JVM-process-global counter, NOT reset per analyze call -- so raw
     :kir data is NOT expected to be identical across separate analyze
     calls when destructuring is used (confirmed live: compiling the same
     destructuring-using source once per backend produced 3 distinct :kir
     values). Harmless for actual compiled behavior (these are local-
     variable names erased to WASM local indices; loop alone, which uses
     the deterministic *loop-counter* instead of gensym, DOES produce
     identical :kir across backends, verified separately) -- but it means
     the existing cross-backend :kir-identity test pattern (established for
     map/get/assoc) does not extend to destructuring as-is; the new test
     suite checks :oracle-value consistency for destructuring instead of
     :kir identity, and documents why"
    "multi-arity defn deferred, not implemented -- see :summary"
    "nested destructuring patterns ([[a] b], {:keys [a]} nested inside a
     vector pattern, etc) are explicitly rejected, one level only, same
     scope limit as documented in the design"]
   :verification
   {:oracle-interpreter "ir.clj's execute -- destructuring (vector/map, let
                          + defn params), vector-as-data, loop/recur (basic,
                          zero-iteration, free-variable capture, nested,
                          cross-defn uniqueness), reproducibility all
                          correct"
    :real-chicory-execution
    "scratch verification (uncommitted, matching compiler/'s existing
     convention), real host-side pair HostFunctions, 8 scenarios: let+map
     bugfix, loop/recur, vector destructuring, map destructuring, defn
     param vector destructuring, defn param map destructuring, multi-loop,
