  :adr/compiler-assoc-remove-fix-2026-07-14
  {:summary "Fixed a known limitation documented in addenda 2/4: assoc only
             ever prepended a new entry, relying on get's first-match-wins
             scan to make the shadowed VALUE correct while the old entry
             stayed as dead weight in the pair-chain -- unbounded growth
             under repeated re-assoc of the same key. Adds
             __kotoba_map_without (same inject-only-when-used pattern as
             __kotoba_map_get) which filters out the old entry before
             assoc prepends the new one."
   :verification
   {:oracle-entry-count
    "wrote a plain count-entries recursion IN .kotoba source itself and
     confirmed a 2-distinct-key map stays at 2 entries after 3 re-assocs of
     the same key (not 5) -- verifies actual dedup, not just that get
     still returns the correct shadowed value (which the OLD buggy code
     already got right)"
    :real-chicory-execution "same scenario re-verified via real Chicory execution (scratch)"
    :test-suite "clojure -M:test: 141 tests / 2841 assertions, 0 failures
                 (includes 6 tests from a concurrently-merged
                 aiueos-freestanding-targets PR, unrelated to this fix)"
    :existing-fuel-test-still-passes-for-a-different-reason
    "map-get-recursion-shares-the-existing-fuel-budget (300x re-assoc ->
     fuel-exhausted) still passes post-fix, but the exhaustion now comes
     from __kotoba_map_without's O(map-size) cost PER assoc call, not from
     get's final scan walking an unboundedly-grown chain -- the assertion
     is unchanged, the underlying mechanism is not"}
   :honest-tradeoff-not-a-pareto-improvement
   "ir.clj/backend/wasm.clj's heap is allocate-only (pair cells are never
    freed/GC'd) -- __kotoba_map_without REBUILDS every surviving entry via
    a fresh (pair (pair-first m) (recurse...)) call, consuming ONE NEW
    heap cell per surviving entry on every single assoc call. This trades
    O(1) heap-cost-per-assoc-call (old, unbounded read-time scan cost) for
    O(map-size) heap-cost-per-assoc-call (new, bounded read-time cost) --
    correct for realistic workloads (occasional writes, frequent reads,
    like the cloud-itonami governor's own access pattern) but NOT a
    strict improvement for a write-heavy-on-a-large-map-with-few-reads
    workload, which could reach heap capacity (pair-capacity, default
    4096) sooner than before. Documented honestly, not silently claimed
    as a pure win."
   :cross-backend-test-adjustment
   "assoc's fix introduces its own gensym'd let-local temp names (assoc-k__/
    assoc-v__) -- same JVM-process-global-counter non-determinism already
    documented for destructuring's temps (addendum 4). The existing
    map-get-assoc-produce-one-shared-kir-across-all-backends test had to
    split: a get-only source still produces byte-identical :kir across all
    4 backends (kept as-is), but an assoc-involving source's raw :kir is
    no longer expected to be identical across backends -- its own new test
    checks :oracle-value consistency instead, same honest pattern as
    addendum 4's destructuring test."
   :cljs-backend-interaction
   "assoc's desugar is a frontend-level change, so it automatically applies
    to the cljs backend added in ADR-2607151500 with zero backend-specific
    code -- re-verified the same entry-count scenario via real nbb
    execution to confirm."
